  "label": "User projected onto the person experiencing a bad day",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the person described in the text who is supposedly having a bad day. The meme uses the visual of the man giving a thumbs-up (a gesture typically associated with positivity) to sarcastically represent the person's bad day, creating a humorous inversion. The text explicitly addresses the user with 'you could be...', directly projecting the user onto the subject of the joke. The user is thus projected onto the 'person' entity, who is the subject of the textual description and the visual representation.",
